---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Picture from '../components/Picture.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Materials"
  description="TPE, STPE, and silicone as used on the companion figures and the expression-head figure in this catalog: what the notes support, and where we stop."
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="page-hero">
      <p class="kicker">Materials</p>
      <h1>TPE, STPE, and silicone — as the notes support.</h1>
      <p class="lead">Silicone companions in this collection are listed as silicone. STPE companions are listed in STPE; a TPE build can be requested and is priced on confirmation. We describe the notes we have, and we stop where those notes stop.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="split top" style="margin-bottom:3.5rem">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>TPE</h2>
        <p>
          Thermoplastic elastomer is a soft skin material widely used on companion bodies. It is slightly tacky before powdering. It can oil over time and is more easily marked than silicone. Care notes for this material usually recommend a mild cleaner and a body powder after washing; see our <a href="/care">care</a> page. A TPE build of an STPE-listed body can be requested. We do not publish a separate TPE price until it is confirmed.
        </p>
        <h2>STPE</h2>
        <p>
          STPE is the material in which the companion bodies at $2,199 are listed. That current price, as of 15 November 2026, is shown beside a previous list price of $2,599. Notes supplied with this material describe less oiling than standard TPE, little odor, and greater durability. That is a claim in those notes. We have not laboratory-tested it, and we will not present it as our own finding.
        </p>
        <h2>Silicone</h2>
        <p>
          The silicone companions in this collection are listed as silicone on a price list dated 4 October 2025, at $1,900 or $1,950. Silicone is generally more stable against oiling than TPE, with a different surface feel, and it is usually cared for with products intended for silicone. The 164 cm expression-head figure is titled as silicone in some notes and described as an STPE body with an expression head in others. We confirm the material of a specific unit before payment.
        </p>
        <h2>Heads, eyes, hair, and skeleton</h2>
        <p>
          These figures combine a body with a chosen head, eye colour, and hair. The 4 October 2025 options sheet for the silicone companions lists three skin tones, six eye colours, implanted hair at +$150, implanted real hair at +$280, and an updated hand option listed as free. A separate note describes a ball-jointed hand skeleton. What is actually fitted to a warehouse unit, or to an order, is confirmed with your inquiry. We do not assume a head from an older pairing note.
        </p>
        <h2>What we show in photographs</h2>
        <p>
          Photographs on product pages stay with the figure they were supplied for. Some of them carry a printed overlay. That overlay is not our product title, and where it disagrees with the specification table, the table is the listing. Collection photographs elsewhere on the site show clothing and finish and are not assigned to a figure. We do not alter photographs to remove overlays.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="frame" style="aspect-ratio:1">
          <Picture
            src="/images/craft/head-sculptures"
            alt="Sculpted head studies — a classical face in dark material, a pale portrait, and a painted head — used here as a craft image, not as a specific product."
            width={1000}
            height={1000}
          />
        </div>
        <p class="photo-caption">Head studies. Not a listing assignment.</p>
        <div class="frame" style="aspect-ratio:4/5;margin-top:1.5rem">
          <Picture
            src="/images/portraits/curly-portrait"
            alt="A close portrait of an adult figure with dark curly hair, looking toward the camera."
            width={1000}
            height={1000}
          />
        </div>
        <p class="photo-caption">Collection photography — illustrative of finish.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
